  "description": "GUFCIV crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C88 H100 Cl2 Dy4 N8 O18 2+,1.5(C2 H6 O1),0.5(H2 O1),Cl1 1-,H1 O1 1-. From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 5 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.529-3.881 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 96.56-111.40°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C182H218Cl6Dy8N16O42. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 2 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
